    {
      "id": "claim_83c830916a864b8fa31f02bd7205b68b",
      "statement": "Every write and read is scoped by containerTag set to the name of the directory under /workspace, sanitized to match ^[a-zA-Z0-9_:-]+$, and never crossed, because that tag is the only boundary preventing one repository's context from leaking into another.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/AGENTS.md#L32-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:29b179e33d01bb67217d3d0b296edcad3d7d13f8baaf2be61dd8bfc88a80b42c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_727359e3a8e5487a84b867dbaa7cd877",
      "statement": "Ingestion is asynchronous: a write returns a status rather than a result and search returns nothing for it until extraction finishes, so a recall missing a fresh write is the queue and must not be retried in a loop; dreaming: instant is used when a memory must be searchable immediately.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/AGENTS.md#L43-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0098f6428f9a5d57adf34b429d51ba0ab4608d0e24f2ae413a7a60ecd6042410:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_63d990924a5a45d6ad00361c54594249",
      "statement": "A queued write can end as status: failed and then be invisible to search, usually because of the engine's own LLM provider rather than the request, so status must be checked before claiming something was remembered and retrying does not help.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/AGENTS.md#L48-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2545dbc6ee70c7614e5001013b1803b9533c2889cf8d8e1ed8ac7dfa45c6282c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_87366cba55fb42adb506bd636255ff66",
      "statement": "customId makes a memory write idempotent, so it should be a stable value derived from what is stored rather than a timestamp.",
